WHATNOW

What tam-edit is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-18, with W3


STATE

  tam-edit is a C11 editor that reproduces micro and links only libtam
  and the C library. The repository started fresh on 2026-11-18 (W3)
  with one commit holding the C11 editor at 1.0.4, on branch dev. The
  old history (the fork of micro, the Go version on master, branches c11
  and test) is archived read-only at greenermoose/tam-edit-micro-fork.
  Commit hashes in older records, review-001.md included, are in that
  archive. VERSION reads 1.0.4 (the footer shows it).

  All five migration milestones are complete (ROADMAP.md, 1.0.0 on
  2026-11-13): editing, views and configuration, syntax highlighting,
  search, encodings, shell, multi-cursor, the parity audit
  (docs/PARITY_AUDIT.md), fuzzing and packaging. Since then: fixes to
  arrow keys, softwrap boundaries, the softwrap goal column, the version
  in the footer, and DeleteWordLeft (W2, 61cc02c0).

  reviews/review-001.md, a review of the cursor code, found eight
  issues. #1 (softwrap goal column after Home/End/word moves, 880cbe4e)
  and #3 (act_delete_word_left multi-cursor and edit pipeline, 61cc02c0)
  are fixed.


NEXT

  1. The open findings of reviews/review-001.md, highest impact first:
     - 2: edit_visual_col and edit_visual_to_rune (src/editor.c) use a
       fixed tab stop of 8 (EDIT_TABSTOP); rendering uses
       config.tabsize. Pass the tab size in.
     - 4: tab-indent stepping in cursor_move_single (src/cursor.c)
       indexes a line by rune column as if it were a byte offset.
     - 7: multi-cursor downstream adjustment can leave secondary cursor
       metadata stale.
     - 5, 6 and 8: empty-document clamp, scroll computed as a render side
       effect, ASCII-only word classes.
     Each fix gets a regression test (make test, make test-asan; make
     test-pty for key paths) and a patch bump. Mark each finding fixed in
     the review with its commit.

